{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#cor:pet-ch5-segments-are-geodesics","title":"cor:pet-ch5-segments-are-geodesics","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.md","line":504,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.tex#cor:pet-ch5-segments-are-geodesics","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#thm:pet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-segment]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.tex","label":"cor:pet-ch5-segments-are-geodesics","line":1023,"source":"\\begin{corollary}[characterization of segments]\n  \\label{cor:pet-ch5-segments-are-geodesics}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0203}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics, prop:pet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers, def:pet-ch5-segment}\n\n  Any piecewise smooth segment is a geodesic.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics,prop:pet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers,def:pet-ch5-segment}\n  \\sketch\n  A segment is a constant-speed length minimizer.  By\n  \\cref{prop:pet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers} it minimizes energy, and\n  \\cref{thm:pet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics} makes it a smooth geodesic.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Corollary</div></section>[characterization of segments] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-636f723a7065742d6368352d7365676d656e74732d6172652d67656f646573696373\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0203</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23thm%3Apet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics\">↗ thm:pet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23prop%3Apet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers\">↗ prop:pet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23def%3Apet-ch5-segment\">↗ def:pet-ch5-segment</a> <p></p>Any piecewise smooth segment is a geodesic.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23thm%3Apet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics\">↗ thm:pet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23prop%3Apet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers\">↗ prop:pet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23def%3Apet-ch5-segment\">↗ def:pet-ch5-segment</a> \\sketch A segment is a constant-speed length minimizer. By <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23prop%3Apet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a7065742d6368352d656e657267792d6c656e6774682d6d696e696d697a657273\">section 4</a> it minimizes energy, and <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23thm%3Apet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#thm:pet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368352d656e657267792d6d696e696d612d67656f646573696373\">section 4</a> makes it a smooth geodesic. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#thm:pet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#rem:pet-ch5-sphere-not-locally-minimizing","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#thm:pet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics","title":"thm:pet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics","label":"thm:pet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers","title":"prop:pet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers","label":"prop:pet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-segment","title":"def:pet-ch5-segment","label":"def:pet-ch5-segment"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-segment-domain-injective","title":"prop:pet-ch5-segment-domain-injective","label":"prop:pet-ch5-segment-domain-injective"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#cor:pet-ch5-segments-are-geodesics","title":"cor:pet-ch5-segments-are-geodesics","tex":"\\begin{corollary}[characterization of segments]\n  \\label{cor:pet-ch5-segments-are-geodesics}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0203}\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics, prop:pet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers, def:pet-ch5-segment}\n\n  Any piecewise smooth segment is a geodesic.\n\\end{corollary}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\uses{thm:pet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics,prop:pet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers,def:pet-ch5-segment}\n  \\sketch\n  A segment is a constant-speed length minimizer.  By\n  \\cref{prop:pet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers} it minimizes energy, and\n  \\cref{thm:pet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics} makes it a smooth geodesic.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#thm:pet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics","title":"thm:pet-ch5-energy-minima-geodesics","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#prop:pet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers","title":"prop:pet-ch5-energy-length-minimizers","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#def:pet-ch5-segment","title":"def:pet-ch5-segment","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}